IMPORT prelude

-- Community Disputes Resolution Act 2015 (Singapore) -- disputes between neighbours: who is a neighbour and what the statutory tort
-- requires (s 4), what follows when a court order is disobeyed (ss 6 to 11), the mandatory treatment order cap (s 12A), the
-- community relations officers' abatement orders, mediation directions and offences (ss 13L, 13N, 13R, 13U, 13W), and the
-- tribunal's jurisdiction, representation and appeal rules (ss 17, 25, 26, 29, 34).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 1/9/2026"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CDRA2015.txt. The revised edition itself "incorporates all amendments up to and including
-- 1 December 2021"; the consolidation annotates later amendments by Act 25 of 2021 (wef 1 April 2022) and Act 43 of 2024 (wef
-- 24 March 2025 and, for ss 12A, 17, 17A, 26(1)(c), 29A, 31A to 31E, wef 1 September 2026).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: noise, smells, clutter, hoarding and obstruction between people who live in
-- the same block or street, and the small-claims-style tribunal that hears them. SCOPED to the rules a resident on either side of a
-- dispute meets. Not encoded: the court's "just and equitable" weighing (s 5(2), s 9(4)), the hoarding order (s 11A) beyond
-- mention, the psychiatric assessment procedure of s 12A beyond its 36-month cap, the officers' appointment and investigation
-- powers (ss 13B to 13K, 13S, 13T), secrecy and regulations (ss 13X to 13ZC), the Director-General's own applications (s 17A),
-- transfer and costs on transfer (ss 20, 21), privacy orders (s 22), settlement registration (s 31A) and civil restraint orders
-- (ss 31B to 31E).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Community Disputes Resolution Act 2015 -- neighbours`

§§ `4(4) and (5) -- who is a neighbour`

-- s 4(4): a neighbour "is an individual who lawfully resides in a place of residence -- (a) that is in the same building as the
-- respondent's place of residence; or (b) that is within 100 metres of the respondent's place of residence, but does not include an
-- individual who occupies the same place of residence as the respondent". Illustrations: flatmates in different rooms, and people in
-- sub-divided units of one apartment with the same registered address, occupy the same place of residence.
-- s 4(5): the distance is measured "from any part of the boundary of one place of residence to any part of the boundary of the other".
-- Whether exactly 100 metres is "within" 100 metres is not said; this encoding treats it as within (an inference).
GIVEN `lawfully resides` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the same building` IS A BOOLEAN, `nearest boundary distance in metres` IS A NUMBER,
      `occupies the same place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a neighbour` IF
        `lawfully resides`
    AND (`in the same building` OR `nearest boundary distance in metres` AT MOST 100)
    AND (NOT `occupies the same place of residence`)

§§ `4(1) and (3) -- the tort`

-- s 4(1): an individual who resides in a place of residence "must not, by his or her act or omission, directly or indirectly, and
-- whether intentionally, recklessly or negligently, cause unreasonable interference with his or her neighbour's enjoyment or use of
-- the place of residence that the neighbour resides in". (2) lists examples "(but is not limited to)": excessive noise, smell, smoke,
-- light or vibration; littering; obstruction; interfering with the neighbour or movable property; surveillance; trespass; and
-- animals. (3): the neighbour "may bring civil proceedings in a court".
-- Reading "whether intentionally, recklessly or negligently" as requiring at least one of the three is an interpretation; the
-- words could also be read as merely making the state of mind irrelevant.
GIVEN `the claimant is a neighbour` IS A BOOLEAN, `the respondent resides in a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the interference is unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN, `intentional` IS A BOOLEAN, `reckless` IS A BOOLEAN, `negligent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tort is made out` IF
        `the claimant is a neighbour`
    AND `the respondent resides in a place of residence`
    AND `the interference is unreasonable`
    AND (`intentional` OR `reckless` OR `negligent`)

§§ `6, 8 and 9 -- when an order is disobeyed`

-- s 5(1): on a claim made out the court may order (a) damages, (b) an injunction, (c) specific performance, (d) an apology.
-- s 6(1), (2): where the respondent fails to comply, the winning party may apply and the court may direct compliance within a
-- specified time if satisfied the respondent "has, without reasonable excuse, failed to comply".
-- s 8: "Section 6 does not apply to an order of court made under section 5 which requires a contravening party to pay damages."
-- s 9(2): a second court may make an exclusion order (excluding the contravening party from his or her own home) if satisfied the
-- party has, without reasonable excuse, failed to comply with a special direction, "and is satisfied that it is just and equitable".
DECLARE Order IS ONE OF
    `an order for damages`
    `an injunction`
    `an order for specific performance`
    `an order to apologise`

GIVEN `the disobeyed order` IS AN Order, `failed to comply` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a special direction may be made` IF
        `failed to comply`
    AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)
    AND CONSIDER `the disobeyed order`
        WHEN `an order for damages` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `failed to comply with the special direction` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `just and equitable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an exclusion order may be made` IF
        `failed to comply with the special direction`
    AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)
    AND `just and equitable`

§§ `6(7), 7 and 10 -- penalties for disobedience`

-- s 6(7): failing to enter into a bond ordered under s 6(3): fine not exceeding $2,000.
-- s 7(1) (special direction) and s 10(1) (exclusion order), in identical terms: "(a) a fine not exceeding $5,000 or ... imprisonment
-- for a term not exceeding 3 months or ... both; and (b) in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $1,000
-- for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction, but not exceeding $10,000 in total".
-- Days are counted as whole numbers here; "part of a day" counts as a day.
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `days the breach continues after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum further fine for a continuing breach of a special direction or exclusion order` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (1000 TIMES `days the breach continues after conviction`) 10000

§§ `11 -- landlords`

-- s 11(1): where the person ordered to enter into a bond under s 6(3) is the landlord of the contravening party's residence, the
-- landlord "is entitled to terminate ... any tenancy relating to that specified residence"; (2) by "written notice which must specify
-- a date of re-possession that is at least 14 days after the date on which the notice is given"; (3) despite any other law or
-- agreement; (4) the landlord "is not liable".
GIVEN `the landlord was ordered to enter into a bond` IS A BOOLEAN, `notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days from notice to re-possession` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the landlord may terminate the tenancy` IF
        `the landlord was ordered to enter into a bond`
    AND `notice is in writing`
    AND `days from notice to re-possession` AT LEAST 14

§§ `12A -- mandatory treatment orders`

-- s 12A(2): the court may order the respondent "to undergo psychiatric treatment for a specified period, but X must not be subject to
-- one or more mandatory treatment orders for a total period longer than 36 months in respect of the same basis". (25): a variation
-- must not extend the period "beyond 36 months after the date the order is first in force". (15), (16): only if the formal
-- assessment report certifies all four matters. In force from 1 September 2026.
GIVEN `total months of treatment ordered on the same basis` IS A NUMBER, `the report certifies all four matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mandatory treatment order is permitted` IF
        `the report certifies all four matters`
    AND `total months of treatment ordered on the same basis` AT MOST 36

§§ `13L -- abatement orders`

-- s 13L(1): the Director-General may issue an abatement order if (a) satisfied the individual (or a co-resident) "was responsible for
-- the act or omission causing unreasonable interference"; (b) a reasonable opportunity to make representations was given; and (c)
-- the individual "was previously issued a written warning to cease ... but failed to do so". (2): (b) and (c) may be skipped where
-- there are reasonable grounds to believe the interference "poses a serious and imminent threat or risk to the mental or physical
-- health or welfare of other persons in the vicinity" and compliance is impracticable -- representations then come "immediately
-- after".
GIVEN `responsible for the interference` IS A BOOLEAN, `given a chance to make representations` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `ignored a prior written warning` IS A BOOLEAN, `serious and imminent threat` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the steps are impracticable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an abatement order may be issued` IF
        `responsible for the interference`
    AND (    (`given a chance to make representations` AND `ignored a prior written warning`)
         OR  (`serious and imminent threat` AND `the steps are impracticable`))

-- s 13L(5): failing without reasonable excuse to comply with an abatement order: "(a) ... a fine not exceeding $10,000 and, in the
-- case of a continuing offence, ... a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day or part of a day ...; and (b) in the case of a
-- second or subsequent conviction, ... a fine not exceeding $20,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 months or ...
-- both" with the same daily further fine. Unlike ss 7 and 10, NO $10,000 total cap on the daily fine is stated.
GIVEN `second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for breaching an abatement order` MEANS
    IF `second or subsequent conviction` THEN 20000 ELSE 10000

GIVEN `second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `imprisonment is available for breaching an abatement order` IF `second or subsequent conviction`

GIVEN `days the breach continues after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum further fine for a continuing breach of an abatement order` MEANS
    1000 TIMES `days the breach continues after conviction`

-- s 13W(1): a person aggrieved by an abatement order "may, within 14 days after receiving the order, appeal ... to the Minister";
-- (2) the order "takes effect and must be complied with" despite the appeal unless the Minister orders otherwise; (5) the
-- Minister's decision is final.
GIVEN `days since receiving the order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal to the Minister is in time` IF `days since receiving the order` AT MOST 14

§§ `13N and 13R -- obstruction and mediation directions`

-- s 13N(1): refusing access to, obstructing, or refusing to comply with a request of an officer without reasonable excuse: fine not
-- exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months or both. (2): "it is not an offence ... to refuse to comply with any
-- request ... by a community relations officer ... who -- (a) fails to declare his or her office; or (b) refuses to produce his or her
-- identification card on demand".
GIVEN `refused the officer's request` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the officer failed to declare office` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer refused to show identification on demand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refusing the officer is an offence` IF
        `refused the officer's request`
    AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)
    AND (NOT `the officer failed to declare office`)
    AND (NOT `the officer refused to show identification on demand`)

-- s 13M(1): an officer may direct the individuals in a neighbour dispute, and their landlord, to mediation "with or without the
-- consent of the persons to be directed"; (4) the direction is final.
-- s 13R(1): a person served a direction "commits an offence if he or she does not attend the mediation"; (2) or if he or she
-- "withdraws from the mediation before the person conducting the mediation ... allows" it; (3) reasonable excuse is a defence for the
-- accused "to prove"; (4) fine not exceeding $1,500.
GIVEN `served a mediation direction` IS A BOOLEAN, `attended` IS A BOOLEAN, `withdrew without the mediator's leave` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mediation direction offence is committed` IF
        `served a mediation direction`
    AND ((NOT `attended`) OR `withdrew without the mediator's leave`)
    AND (NOT `proved a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `13U and 34 -- composition`

-- s 13U(1)(a) (offences under Part 2A) and s 34(1)(a) (other offences), in the same words: a sum "not exceeding the lower of ...
-- (i) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (ii) $2,000". Only offences prescribed as
-- compoundable may be compounded; none is prescribed in the Act itself.
GIVEN `the maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`the maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 2000

§§ `17 and 19 -- the tribunal's jurisdiction`

-- s 17(3): "the tribunal's jurisdiction does not extend to a claim under section 4 -- (a) which exceeds the prescribed limit; or
-- (b) which is brought more than 2 years after the cause of action has accrued". (4): the claimant may abandon the excess, and then
-- the claim is within the limit but no remedy may exceed it and the order fully discharges the claim. (5): the prescribed limit "is
-- $20,000" unless the Minister substitutes another amount. s 19: no splitting a claim to bring each part under the limit.
-- Two years is counted here in whole months (at most 24 months is in time).
GIVEN `amount claimed` IS A NUMBER, `months since the cause of action accrued` IS A NUMBER, `abandons the excess` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tribunal has jurisdiction` IF
        (`amount claimed` AT MOST 20000 OR `abandons the excess`)
    AND `months since the cause of action accrued` AT MOST 24

GIVEN `amount claimed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the tribunal can award` MEANS
    `the lesser of` `amount claimed` 20000

§§ `25, 26 and 29 -- costs, lawyers and appeals`

-- s 25: "costs, other than disbursements, must not be granted to or awarded against any party".
-- s 29(1): a party "must present his or her own case". (3): "no party (other than the Director-General) ... may be represented by an
-- advocate and solicitor unless -- (a) all the parties ... otherwise agree ...; and (b) the Registrar or tribunal ... grants
-- permission". (4): no other agent, paid or not, except the persons in (2) (parents of minors, the old, illiterate or infirm, etc.).
GIVEN `the party is the Director-General` IS A BOOLEAN, `all parties agree` IS A BOOLEAN, `the tribunal permits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a lawyer may represent the party` IF
        `the party is the Director-General`
    OR  (`all parties agree` AND `the tribunal permits`)

-- s 26(1): an appeal lies to the General Division of the High Court "only" (a) on a question of law; (b) on the ground that the
-- claim was outside jurisdiction; (c) against an order under s 6(2) or (3), 9(2), 11A, 12A, 31B to 31E; or (d) against a final order.
-- (2): "only if permission to appeal is given by a tribunal"; (3) the grant or refusal is final. s 28: the High Court's decision is
-- final. s 27: an appeal does not stay enforcement unless ordered.
GIVEN `on a question of law` IS A BOOLEAN, `claim was outside jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `against a listed order` IS A BOOLEAN, `against a final order` IS A BOOLEAN, `the tribunal gave permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal lies to the High Court` IF
        `the tribunal gave permission`
    AND (`on a question of law` OR `claim was outside jurisdiction` OR `against a listed order` OR `against a final order`)
